    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94815.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 68,
    "turn_text": "well we're just on the front end of this investigate we've got a number of investigations on the censorship of speech and and f b i was a blower's coming forward different things but we're just on the front end of this it started when we had an f b i was a blower come tell us that around january six two twenty uh... twenty one that there was an email between the government and federal government and bank of america saying we want you bank of america to give us all debit and credit card purchases on uh... in and around january six So a specific time frame at a specific location here in the DC area. And we thought that was unusual. But then they also said, and we want you to overlay that with any purchase at any time of any firearm. And so we had an agent who said he thought there was no predicate for soliciting this type of information. It was done, we think, without any process, so no legal process. And this agent said this was inappropriate and didn't want to use this, but he brought it to our attention. And then from there, we've learned, as you pointed out, that there are some of these online transactions, you can put a message in with it, and they were asking banks to search their customer's database for certain key terms at the suggestion of the federal government, terms like MAGA, Patriot, Trump, those kind of things. And then also they were flagging just specific purchases at specific places. So if you shop at Cabellas, which is half the people of Michigan and up the same in Ohio, I mean, you shop at that Bass Pro Shoppers, they were flagging those as well. So it's kind of creepy. We're just on the front end of this, but we're going to continue to dig.",
